/**
 * Natur & geografi → Ekologi & miljö → Miljöpolitik & samhälle, 2951–2957 (0.46): environmental goals, environmental
 * law, protected areas, climate agreements, environmental impact assessment, sustainable transport and citizens'
 * environmental choices.
 * Recurring signs: a green leaf or a small green globe means "the environment"; a target means a goal; a thick book with
 * § is a law; a clipboard and a magnifying glass mean checking; gold coins are money; a calendar with a red ring is a
 * deadline; a green shield means "protected"; a red ring with a bar means "not allowed"; flags in plain made-up colours
 * stand for different countries. The thing the word names is coloured and ringed in orange, while the rest is pale or
 * grey; abstract words are small symbolic scenes where the coloured idea dominates and a grey copy stands beside it as
 * contrast. Digits and § only; no words, no brands, no party symbols, no logos of real organisations, no real flags and
 * no pointing fingers.
 */
